<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tessĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		tessera, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to</i>
			tesserae. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars,</span>”
				<i>the art of dice-playing</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 6, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">28, 4, 21</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tessĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A dice-thrower</i>, <i>dice-player</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 4, 21</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 624,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>He who receives and distributes the watchword from
				the commander</i> (v. tessera, II.), <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 1,
			25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 2, 7</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3462</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">3471</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3480</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
